Summary?:=A0 cmevla and brivla are separate morphological classes (ends in =
a consonant/ doesn't, for short).=A0=20
brivla can occur anywhere cmevla can occur.=A0=20
as of now, cmevla alone cannot occur in=A0 primary brivla positions (selbri=
, seltau, tertau).
as a practical matter, it would be useful to allow cmevla to occur at least=
 in tanru, since there are many name+predicate combinations in science, etc=
.=20
but most of these are names, again, not predicates, and so already allowed.

merging the two classes syntactically would mean one less syntactic class, =
but not obviously simplify the language otherwise.



